Subject: [PATCH] Make undo/redo shortcuts follow the letter Z on any keyboard
 layout

Key bindings refer to the physical key position (US layout), so on e.g.
a German (QWERTZ) keyboard the default undo shortcut was Ctrl + the key
labeled Y. When the keyboard layout is known, move the default undo/redo
bindings to the key that has the letter Z. Bindings changed by the user
are left alone.

The Edit menu's Undo/Redo now show the user's actual undo/redo key
bindings (display only on Windows/Linux, where the renderer handles the
keys).

Fork-Change: 06-undo-z-on-any-layout
